    "problem_statement": "UnboundLocalError when using retry decorators\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using tenacity retry decorators, an `UnboundLocalError` is raised for the variable `fut` in the `_begin_iter` method. This appears to happen when the retry logic attempts to access the `fut` variable before it's properly defined.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tenacity\n\n@tenacity.retry(stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(3))\ndef failing_function():\n    raise Exception(\"This will fail\")\n\ntry:\n    failing_function()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\nThe error occurs with various retry configurations and affects basic retry functionality.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe retry decorator should work normally, attempting the function the specified number of times before raising a RetryError.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'fut' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThis error prevents the retry mechanism from working at all, making the library unusable for basic retry scenarios."
  },
